# Prototype

This is the first version of my line follower. The goal is to get the basic hardware working before moving on to a custom PCB and chassis.

For this prototype, I'll be using the components I already have instead of designing everything from scratch immediately.

## Hardware

* ESP32 development board
* QTR-8RC line sensor
* L298N motor driver
* Two DC motors
* Battery and connecting wires

## Goals

* Get the QTR-8RC sensor working with the ESP32.
* Read the sensor values and check how it responds to black and white surfaces.
* Get both motors running through the L298N.
* Combine the sensor and motor systems.
* Implement a basic PID controller for line following.
* Test the robot and record what works and what needs improvement.

## Why start with a prototype?

I want to test the basic idea and understand the hardware before designing a custom PCB. This should help me find wiring or software problems early instead of having to debug everything after making the PCB.

## Status

The prototype is currently in development. I'll update this section as I complete each stage and add test results.
